From: taimen camera bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] soft ISP: contrast autofocus

Add a sharpness statistic (sum of absolute horizontal green gradients)
to the CPU stats for 10-bit packed Bayer, and a contrast hill-climb Af
algorithm in the soft IPA: coarse scan, fine scan, lock, rescan on a
sustained sharpness drop. The Af drives the lens through the existing
sensor-controls path with V4L2_CID_FOCUS_ABSOLUTE; the simple pipeline
splits that control out to the CameraLens. Enabled per sensor via the
tuning file (imx362 only; the front imx179 is fixed-focus).

--- a/include/libcamera/internal/software_isp/swisp_stats.h
+++ b/include/libcamera/internal/software_isp/swisp_stats.h
@@ -43,6 +43,11 @@
 	 * \brief A histogram of luminance values of all the sampled pixels
 	 */
 	Histogram yHistogram;
+	/**
+	 * \brief Sum of absolute horizontal green gradients of the sampled
+	 *        pixels, a contrast-autofocus sharpness measure
+	 */
+	uint64_t sharpness;
 };
 
 } /* namespace libcamera */
